PCI: pcie_acs_override: let id: entries opt in past external_facing

The zen ACS override refuses to touch any device that is untrusted or
external_facing, which excludes everything behind a Thunderbolt/USB4
tunnel -- the AMD tunnel root ports are marked external_facing by ACPI
and pci_set_untrusted() propagates untrusted to every device enumerated
below them. On islandfox that puts the USB4 tunnel port, both Alpine
Ridge bridges, the ConnectX-4 Lx PF and all of its VFs in one IOMMU
group, so no VF can be handed to a guest.

Check the explicit id: list before that bail so a named vendor:device
can opt in, while downstream/multifunction keep refusing external ports.

--- a/drivers/pci/quirks.c
+++ b/drivers/pci/quirks.c
@@ -5172,6 +5172,12 @@
 	if (!pci_is_pcie(dev) || dev->acs_cap)
 		return -ENOTTY;
 
+	/* Explicit id: entries opt in, external-facing or not */
+	for (i = 0; i < max_acs_id; i++)
+		if (acs_on_ids[i].vendor == dev->vendor &&
+		    acs_on_ids[i].device == dev->device)
+			return 1;
+
 	if (dev->untrusted || dev->external_facing)
 		return -ENOTTY;
 
